WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.540
Hello and welcome back to JD science.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.360
Today we are exploring plant tissues and organs.

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.920
A leaf has several tissues.

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.300
The epidermis covers the leaf.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.740
The palisade mesophyll is packed with chloroplasts for photosynthesis.

6
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.420
The spongy mesophyll has air spaces for gas exchange.

7
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.080
Xylem and phloem form the veins.

8
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.480
Guard cells control the stomata which control gas exchange and

9
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.140
water loss.

10
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.360
Water evaporates through the stomata which pulls water up

11
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.140
the xylem.

12
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.740
This is transpiration.

13
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.060
Transpiration is faster in warm, dry, windy conditions

14
00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.300
and in bright light.

15
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.600
Xylem carries water and mineral ions upwards.

16
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.760
Phloem carries sugars up and down the plant.

17
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.340
Transpiration is the loss of water vapour from leaves, mainly through

18
00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:50.900
stomata.

19
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.040
Water evaporates from mesophyll cell surfaces and diffuses

20
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:55.860
into the air.

21
00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.920
This creates tension that helps draw a continuous column of water

22
00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:00.960
up the xylem.

23
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.800
Phloem transports dissolved sugars from sources such as photosynthesising

24
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:09.220
leaves to sinks such as roots and growing fruits.

25
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.060
The direction depends on the location of sources and sinks.

26
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:17.260
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

27
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.120
your own words.

28
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.780
Focus on what happens, why it happens and how

29
00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.240
the structures involved help the process work.

30
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.120
Now, pause the video and try this exam style question.

31
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.480
Name the plant tissue that carries sugars and describe the direction it

32
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:33.100
carries them.

33
00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.600
Here is a model answer.

34
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.240
Phloem, it carries sugars up and down the plant.

35
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.700
If this explanation has helped, please subscribe to JD Science for

36
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.300
more lessons.

37
00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:48.260
You can find further learning resources and practice questions at

38
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.380
jdscience .co .uk.

39
00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:51.780
Thank you for watching.
